  "verdict": "**\"NO TIMING ANYWHERE\" IS VOID: IT WAS ONE TRAINING SEED.** The old checkpoint's pipe-2 lift is -0.026. Re-running **its own recipe** -- 3,000 steps, batch 128, same architecture, corpus, split, loss -- gives +0.028, POSITIVE. And at 15,000 steps it is positive in 3/3 seeds (median +0.130, range +0.063 to +0.177), every interval excluding zero. **Four freshly trained checkpoints all show a positive pipe-2 timing lift; the one the conclusion was built on is the outlier.** The fifty-first block measured a single checkpoint and \u00a71 re-measured that same checkpoint, so neither read caught it -- the ledger's own rule that one seed is a screen was the thing being violated. **The policy does discriminate when to jump where it succeeds. The observation is not the indicated lever, and there is also a training-length dose-response on top of the seed effect: +0.028 at 3k against a median +0.130 at 15k.**",
  "minutes": 0.4
